OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan remediation (blocking findings from review v1): (1) CENSUS expanded — grep 'mode=\"structured\"' under src/rebar/llm/ yields these live consumers now all enumerated in AC-1/Scope: findings.py, enrich.py, epic_bug_screen.py, overlap/judge.py, evals/eval_solver.py, workflow/completion_recovery.py, workflow/runs.py, plan_review/{passes,xcheck,prerequisites,completion_subcall}.py, code_review/{registry,workflow_ops}.py, plus runner.py itself. (2) structured_retry_limit=0 fail-safe: the knob is RETAINED (output_retry_allowance clamps retries+UsageLimits addend, structured_run.py:158-159); overlap/judge.py:212 and contracts.py:223 batch abstain survive — added as a dedicated AC + test. (3) AC-3 reworded: the old 'more than one outer Agent run' oracle contradicted the bug-895c native->prompted downgrade (two legit run_sync calls). New AC-3 counts bespoke fresh-Agent output-attempt LOOP reconstructions: exactly ONE run on a well-formed first response; exactly TWO only on the 895c downgrade; never a third.","timestamp":1786976376731010001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan remediation v2->v5: census made ROBUST. A literal RunRequest(mode=\"structured\") grep matched ZERO sites (multi-line constructions) and missed computed-mode consumers (plan_review/fidelity_spot_eval.py:101 sets mode via a conditional). AC-1 pivoted to the structural invariant (single PydanticAIRunner facade + single-sourced structured dispatch) verified by a mode-RESOLVING AST census over src/ + scripts/, not a text grep. Added consumers fidelity_spot_eval.py and scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py. AC-3 now counts agent.run_sync invocations (1 happy / 2 on 895c downgrade), not Agent constructions. Softened output_retry_allowance mechanism-pinning to observable allowance-clamp behavior.","timestamp":1786977709740963001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC-6 canary (operator-attested) BLOCKED — deferred: the direct-Anthropic + Bedrock same-run cache canaries require live provider credentials (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY + AWS creds) that are NOT available in this autonomous session. All autonomous ACs done: AC-1 (single-sourced dispatch + mode-resolving AST census), AC-2 (RP-01 matrix green), AC-3 (no-bespoke-loop: run_sync counting), AC-4 (structured_retry_limit=0 single-shot), AC-5 (fallback/provenance/shape regressions green), AC-7 (lint/typecheck/module-size/complexity), AC-8 (docs). AC-6 left [operator-attested] unchecked per honest-attestation policy; a human operator with creds must run the cache canaries and record model ids + cache read/write/input counts + complete/omit branch on this ticket.","timestamp":1786979971952852001}],"created_at":1786924779290617001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b17d659f-c55b-4eff-bd00-de5c3fe604a4","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"558e-d9bd-e285-40a1"},{"link_uuid":"45803415-b082-42b4-b166-4c5021e01564","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2e1b-6517-eb1e-4309"},{"link_uuid":"9bbf1a86-8d21-4c82-97af-6c3f6f71fc40","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c508-867d-8bf5-48ef"},{"link_uuid":"9bf5fcce-c9be-40fb-a365-a62a6c5eb65f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6ef6-967f-5784-4872"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe approved Pydantic output, bounded-operation, compatibility, and candidate-tracing children establish the replacement behavior [rebar:serge-monotonous-aruanas] [rebar:amoebaean-hemihedral-vervet]. S2 already converted `_pai_structured` to ONE bounded Pydantic `Agent` run per output mode (native / prompted); this final change makes that one-operation path AUTHORITATIVE for EVERY `mode=\"structured\"` consumer (library, CLI, MCP, and every in-tree caller), proves provider-cache behavior, then removes the obsolete manual retry machinery and any temporary compatibility delegation — WITHOUT breaking patch/import seams and WITHOUT regressing the `structured_retry_limit=0` single-shot fail-safe.\n\n## Approach\nSwitch every structured `PydanticAIRunner` consumer to the one-operation path through the existing facade. Preserve `ProviderSession`, candidate order, output-mode policy, tool surfaces, timeout/transport limits, provenance, and serialized verdict shapes. `structured_retry_limit` is RETAINED as the output-retry-allowance cap. The single allowance `N = output_retry_allowance(req) = min(OUTPUT_RETRIES, max(0, structured_retry_limit))` (structured_run.py:147) seeds BOTH budgets: the Agent `retries={\"output\":N}` (apply_structured_seams, :183) AND the CONSTRUCTED request budget — `build_usage_limits` sets `UsageLimits(request_limit=req_limit + allowance)` (structured_run.py:429-431). The RETURNED bare `req_limit` EXCLUDES that addend (it feeds telemetry and `iteration_limit_for`'s `2*B` inverse), so the addend lives ONLY in the constructed `UsageLimits`; the returned/logged `req_limit` is not the model-turn ceiling. Seeding both from one N guarantees the request budget can NEVER trip before the output-retry counter, so `structured_retry_limit=0` → single-shot (zero output-repair retries AND zero addend) — the overlap/judge.py:212 and contracts.py:223 abstain fail-safe. Both branches (`_run_native_output`, `_run_prompted_output`) are ONE `agent.run_sync` with pydantic-ai's IN-Agent `retries`; the prompted path's tolerant-parse+validator failure is fed back via `ModelRetry` INSIDE that single run (NOT a bespoke Python loop), so a bounded retry adds a model request without a second `run_sync`. Run the complete ticket/test oracle and authorized direct Anthropic plus Bedrock cache canaries before deletion. S2 already removed the bespoke scheduler, so no obsolete attempt-loop or compatibility delegation remains to delete (a re-runnable census asserts this); retain deterministic parsing (`structured.py`), the runner facade, and public/re-export paths. Document the retry layers, request budget, complete-or-omit history, trace-not-usage candidates, and the raise-the-limit follow-up policy.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py`, `src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py`, `src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py` — authoritative call-site cutover and obsolete-scheduler removal.\n- `src/rebar/llm/structured.py` — retain pure repair and stop/refusal policy; remove only dead retry integration.\n- ALL in-tree `mode=\"structured\"` consumers (exhaustive census enumerated in AC-1 and the pinned comment; incl. computed-mode `plan_review/fidelity_spot_eval.py` and out-of-tree `scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py`) — compatibility verification, no call-site rewrite needed since all already route through the `get_runner(...).run()` facade.\n- `docs/llm-framework.md`, `docs/reuse-surface.md` — documented runtime and library contracts.\n- The RP-01 focused runner, structured-output, fallback, usage, failure, cache, plan-review, code-review, and completion suites.\n\n## Testing\n- Run the recovered RP-01 behavior matrix and all focused historical ticket regressions.\n- Consumer census (robust, NOT literal-grep): a re-runnable AST scan over `src/` and `scripts/` resolves each `RunRequest(...)` construction's EFFECTIVE `mode` — constant-folding computed values like `fidelity_spot_eval.py`'s `mode = \"structured\" if ... else \"findings\"` and matching multi-line constructions a single-line grep misses — enumerates every structured consumer and asserts none submits structured work except through the `get_runner(...).run(...)` facade; paired with a runtime contract test that the runner's structured dispatch is single-sourced (one implementation, no bespoke scheduler).\n- `structured_retry_limit=0` fail-safe: a test asserts the knob still yields zero output-repair retries (single Agent output attempt), preserving overlap/judge.py:212 and the contracts.py:223 batch abstain.\n- AC-3 invariant: a test asserts exactly ONE outer Agent run on a well-formed first response, and exactly TWO (native then prompted) only on the bug-895c downgrade — never a third.\n- Run lean/full import, lint, typecheck, complexity, and module-size gates.\n- Run direct Anthropic and Bedrock same-run retry canaries using environment-provided credentials without printing or persisting secrets; record cache read/write/input counts and complete-versus-omitted wire observations on the ticket.\n- Confirm rollback by temporarily selecting the pre-removal compatibility commit against the same fixtures; no stored data migration is involved.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The one-operation Pydantic path is the SOLE structured-output implementation reachable through the `PydanticAIRunner` facade, so EVERY `mode=\"structured\"` consumer — library, CLI, MCP, and each in-tree caller in the exhaustive census (`plan_review/{__init__,passes,xcheck,prerequisites,completion_subcall,fidelity_spot_eval}`, `code_review/workflow_ops`, `overlap/judge`, `enrich`, `epic_bug_screen`, `evals/eval_solver`, `workflow/completion_recovery`, `workflow/runs`, `scripts/jira_dc_capability_map`) — necessarily uses it; verified by consumer contract tests, by a mode-resolving AST census (not a literal grep) that fails if any structured `RunRequest` is submitted outside `get_runner(...).run(...)`, and by a runner contract test that structured dispatch is single-sourced.\n- [x] The recovered RP-01 behavior matrix passes with only the approved deltas: shared request exhaustion, bounded output-size retry, complete-or-omit failed response, aggregate successful-run usage, exact causal restoration, and candidate tracing outside usage.\n- [x] No bespoke fresh-Agent output-attempt loop remains — output repair is the in-Agent bounded retry (`retries={\"output\":N}`), not a scheduler reconstructing an Agent per attempt. A structured call whose first response is well-formed performs EXACTLY ONE outer model run; the ONLY sanctioned second is the bug-895c native->prompted downgrade. The oracle counts `agent.run_sync` invocations (the outer model runs), NOT `Agent` constructions: exactly one on the happy path, exactly two (native then prompted) on the 895c downgrade, never a third.\n- [x] `structured_retry_limit` is retained as the output-retry-allowance cap; `structured_retry_limit=0` yields zero output-repair retries (single-shot), preserving the overlap/judge.py and contracts.py batch abstain fail-safe; verified by a dedicated test.\n- [x] Existing provider fallback eligibility/order, tool limits, timeout/transport ownership, provenance, final artifact policy, and serialized output shapes remain green in their historical regression suites.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Direct Anthropic and Bedrock canaries pass with secrets absent from output and artifacts; the ticket records timestamp, model ids, request counts, cache read/write/input counts, complete/omit branch, and successful typed result.\n- [x] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, the focused suite, module-size gate, and complexity ratchet pass with `runner.py` at or below 800 lines and every new module between 100 and 500 lines.\n- [x] The documented retry-layer and accounting contracts match runtime behavior, including the normal plan-reviewed follow-up to raise the shared allowance if legitimate recovery is starved.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_rp01_s5_authoritative_oracle.py","reason":"Held-out invariant oracle: single-sourced structured dispatch (AC-1), in-Agent bounded retry vs no-loop (AC-3), structured_retry_limit=0 single-shot fail-safe (AC-4)."},{"path":"docs/llm-framework.md","reason":"AC-7: document the three structured retry layers and their accounting, complete-or-omit history, trace-not-usage candidates, raise-the-limit follow-up policy."},{"path":"docs/reuse-surface.md","reason":"AC-7: document the one-bounded-operation structured contract and structured_retry_limit on the RunRequest reuse seam."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","2e1b-6517-eb1e-4309"],["depends_on","558e-d9bd-e285-40a1"],["parent","905d-1287-effc-4a83"],["relates_to","6ef6-967f-5784-4872"],["relates_to","c508-867d-8bf5-48ef"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"905d-1287-effc-4a83","parent_status_uuid":"04035cc0-ee18-4c90-9a25-5b6fafe1cba0","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["janitor","rp01","llm","cutover"],"ticket_id":"10a3-7dd0-1b3d-47cc","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-01 S5 — Cut over runner consumers and remove bespoke structured-output retries","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["cc7c99be-e295-4f23-bd4b-2a746ffcf8e3","13eaf90c-7f40-4b7a-99b7-6f9d7c8ed41f","8712769a-b644-416c-9042-8261319bca11","ac184985-9c96-4b40-b602-d079fce5bfff","5e183070-fee1-4c5d-8d77-18620daf334e","9526fc09-3e0b-4dd2-b7f3-8c16196c50df","470094ec-e26d-46b7-b92b-f293839bbcf3","34fb83ff-500e-4d21-b24d-ca3dfb3f9665","04035cc0-ee18-4c90-9a25-5b6fafe1cba0","ab822b70-f2bd-4754-ab05-18a92cc6be9f","70df0c96-e992-4919-bc9f-4e1a6d3428b7","f04f32af-fb71-4f76-9229-0dd9b5bca8f7","caf31a7b-36c0-4614-b29c-cffb2ddbf6f9","71a02768-8036-4887-8bef-a289ab94c088","26fa7fe6-d5f1-4f1b-80a8-a0ae0df8c68e","434d5816-5a42-4b8c-9c2b-468e34a84d51","22ace380-4e59-4de7-b179-bd08e6c3561c","2e978a19-6bfa-4e8a-a286-45b63c1936f7","9bbf1a86-8d21-4c82-97af-6c3f6f71fc40","9bf5fcce-c9be-40fb-a365-a62a6c5eb65f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786981176663412066,"uuid":"339da178-2548-4076-a39a-848b251141ce"}